------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the engine setup script installs on the user's machine
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

engine-setup/install-engine.ps1 downloads and installs, into a folder chosen by
the user, software that keeps its own licence and is not redistributed by Mia.
Mia talks to ComfyUI over HTTP on 127.0.0.1 and runs its own Python worker in
the same environment. Versions are pinned in engine-setup/versions.txt,
engine-setup/custom_nodes.txt and engine-setup/constraints.txt.

uv (https://github.com/astral-sh/uv), MIT OR Apache-2.0.
  The Python installer and package manager; its release archive is downloaded
  from GitHub.
CPython (https://www.python.org/), PSF License Agreement (SPDX: Python-2.0).
  Python 3.13, installed by uv from Astral's python-build-standalone builds
  (https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone), which also contain
  libraries under their own licences.
ComfyUI (https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI), GPL-3.0.
ComfyUI-LTXVideo (https://github.com/Lightricks/ComfyUI-LTXVideo),
  LTX-2 Community License Agreement.
ComfyUI-Video-Depth-Anything
  (https://github.com/yuvraj108c/ComfyUI-Video-Depth-Anything), Apache-2.0.
ComfyUI-SeedVR2_VideoUpscaler
  (https://github.com/numz/ComfyUI-SeedVR2_VideoUpscaler), Apache-2.0.
PyTorch (https://pytorch.org/), BSD-3-Clause.
PyAV (https://github.com/PyAV-Org/PyAV), BSD-3-Clause.
imageio-ffmpeg (https://github.com/imageio/imageio-ffmpeg), BSD-2-Clause,
  which provides an FFmpeg binary (https://ffmpeg.org/) under LGPL/GPL.
The other Python packages listed in engine-setup/requirements-mia.txt, each
  under its own licence.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

tools/fixtures/comfy_object_info.json is test data only and is not packaged with
Mia. It is a dump of ComfyUI's /object_info: node names, inputs and tooltips
from ComfyUI (GPL-3.0) and from the custom nodes ComfyUI-LTXVideo (LTX-2
Community License), ComfyUI-SeedVR2_VideoUpscaler and
ComfyUI-Video-Depth-Anything (Apache-2.0), each under its own licence; personal
model and input file lists were removed.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Mia does not ship any model weights. Models are downloaded by the user, from
their original publishers, through Mia's model library or by hand, and remain
under their own licences (LTX-2.x Community License for LTX-2.5, LTX-2
Community License for the LTX-2.3 IC-LoRAs, Apache-2.0, MIT, and others; see
README.md, section "Models"). Mia shows each model's licence flag: MiniMax
H3 is offered with an "R&D only" flag; models whose licence is non-commercial or
excludes the European Union are recognised but never offered in a block.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fonts
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The interface uses Segoe UI Variable and Cascadia Mono as installed with
Windows. No font file is distributed with Mia.
